description:
We are CDAI—the data and artificial intelligence engine of Compass Group North America. We design and deliver custom, in\-house solutions tailored to the unique complexities of food service and hospitality. Our work is grounded in strong data foundations, layered with AI to enhance forecasting, streamline operations, and enable better, faster decision\-making across Compass Group. With deep integration into the business and a commitment to white\-glove service, CDAI empowers associates, clients, and customers through innovative, future\-forward technologies.

**Job Summary**
---------------


Job Summary We are seeking a strategic and hands\-on AI Manager to lead our dynamic team of engineers and scientists in building innovative AI solutions. The ideal candidate combines technical expertise with strong leadership skills, excels in cross\-functional collaboration, and is passionate about translating advanced AI capabilities into real\-world impact. As an AI Manager, you will guide the development of advanced data products and AI\-powered applications, while shaping the roadmap, processes, and talent that drive long\-term success. You will partner closely with stakeholders across Engineering, Data Science, Product, and Business teams to ensure scalable, production\-grade outcomes.



Now, if you were to come on board as our AI Manager, we’d ask you to do the following:

* Oversee the design, development, and deployment of scalable AI solutions across the organization;
* Provide strategic direction for AI initiatives while ensuring alignment with business objectives;
* Manage and mentor a multidisciplinary team of AI Engineers, ML Engineers, and Data Scientists;
* Lead technical architecture decisions, system design, and solution reviews;
* Foster a culture of engineering excellence, code quality, and continuous improvement;
* Collaborate with Product and Engineering leaders to scope features and prioritize development efforts;
* Stay informed on cutting\-edge AI advancements (e.g., LLMs, RAG, vector databases) and evaluate their practical application within the company;
* Establish best practices and frameworks for model development, MLOps, and scalable deployment;
* Present complex AI concepts and project outcomes to technical and non\-technical stakeholders.



Think you have what it takes to be our AI Manager? Here’s how we’ll know:

* 5\+ years of hands\-on experience delivering AI / data products, including at least 2 years in a leadership role;
* Deep technical expertise in areas such as Large Language Models (LLMs), Retrieval\-Augmented Generation (RAG), embeddings, and vector search;
* Strong software engineering fundamentals, including experience with Python and data science tools (NumPy, pandas, etc.);
* Proven track record of deploying AI models into production in cloud\-based environments (AWS, GCP, or Azure);
* Experience managing teams and projects in agile environments with strong prioritization skills;
* Familiarity with modern data platforms, database systems (SQL \& NoSQL), and RESTful APIs;
* Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to explain AI concepts to non\-technical audiences;
* A growth mindset, with a passion for mentoring, coaching, and developing high\-performing teams.

Compass Group Canada is committed to nurturing a diverse workforce representative of the communities within which we operate. We encourage and are pleased to consider all qualified candidates, without regard to race, colour, citizenship, religion, sex, marital / family status, sexual orientation, gender identity, aboriginal status, age, disability or persons who may require an accommodation, to apply.



For accommodation requests during the hiring process, please contact PeopleHub@compass\-canada.com for further information.

Overview:

Groupe Dynamite Inc. (GDI) is a Montréal\-based, public company of integrated omni\-channel brands, designing and distributing accessible, trend\-forward fashion for women since 1975\.  

Our mission of "Empowering YOU to be YOU, one outfit at a time" is brought to life through the GARAGE and DYNAMITE banners and represents the consumer\-centric core of GDI's long\-standing success as a leading retailer in North America.  

Today, GDI operates nearly 300 stores across Canada and the United States, as well as shoppable brand experiences at Garageclothing.com and Dynamiteclothing.com. **Job Summary:**
Join our Data Science team, a product\-driven innovation hub reshaping the online and in\-store shopping experience. As the Data \& AI Product Lead, you’ll own the development and delivery of data science products that have real, measurable business impact. You’ll bridge the gap between business needs and technical execution, ensuring that every solution we build is deployed, adopted, and continuously improved. Working closely with colleagues across E\-commerce and brick and mortar, you’ll help bring next\-generation data products from concept to production, enhancing forecasting, allocation, and the customer experience. **Responsibilities*** Define and lead the day\-to\-day strategy and roadmap for data science products, including quarterly planning and milestone presentations;
* Translate complex business challenges into actionable product requirements and prioritize and document initiatives using Jira and Confluence;
* Collaborate with cross\-functional teammates, including data scientists, engineers, QA, analysts, and business stakeholders to bring products from concept to production;
* Own the product backlog and sprint planning to ensure alignment with Agile best practices and strategic milestones;
* Oversee the end\-to\-end lifecycle of AI and data products, ensuring quality, scalability, and successful adoption;
* Establish and track success metrics to guide post\-launch iteration and continuous improvement;
* Communicate ideas, progress, and impact clearly across both technical and business teams.

 **Qualifications*** 5\+ years of experience in product management or delivery in data/AI, with a proven track record of bringing products from development to production;
* Demonstrated ability to manage, iterate, and scale data science products to ensure lasting adoption and business impact;
* Strong hands\-on experience with Jira, Confluence, and Agile frameworks for managing product cycles;
* Solid understanding of end\-to\-end data science development workflows, including problem framing, data analysis, and performance monitoring;
* Highly organized, analytical, and outcome\-driven, with a focus on delivering measurable value;
* Exceptional communication and stakeholder management skills, comfortable translating between technical and business audiences;
* Experience in retail, fashion, or supply chain is a strong asset, but not required.



At GDI, you will be part of a growing organization that understands the importance of investing in people and offers you:* A comprehensive compensation package that includes performance\-driven bonuses;
* A group retirement savings program with employer matching;
* Flexible group insurance with personalized coverage that meets your needs;
* An employee discount at Garage and Dynamite;
* Exclusive private sample sales;
* A flexible vacation policy;
* And more!



GDI has been repeatedly voted one of Montréal’s Top Employers and one of Canada’s Top Employers for Young People. **Our promise…**  

No day will be like the last—we aim to be better today than we were yesterday. We are committed to employment equity.  

Candidates that are retained will be called for an interview.  

\#LI\-NM1
